From 678f77b35384b7918605e20f5c0b7e3593cd8dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:52:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/47] Z 6III: the touch panel -- a controller on I2C bank 0,
 EXT_INT_14, and -machine touch

The rear monitor's touch panel had no device. Its driver
(0x40cc1aa0-0x40cc3300) feeds the touch input service TPIS
(0x40d2bf70.., the gestures TouchOn/Slide/Flick/Pinch), and is wired by
its init sub_40CC20A8 through the runtime tables:

  I2C        handle sub_40C00460(0) -> bank 0; slave 0x55
  interrupt  resource 0x2d, pin {port 3, bit 14}, line record {bank 1,
             bit 5, INTID 69} = EXT_INT_14, falling edge, callback
             0x40cc21c8 (flag bit 0 of 0xa030582e8)
  power      resource 0x8c, pin {port 9, bit 15}, 1 = on

The driver's task (sub_40CC1BA8) waits for an interrupt and reads
register 0x10 (2 bytes: records, flags); the first interrupt after power
is taken only with flags bit 7 (0x40cc1e64), after which it writes
02/01 to start scanning and its configuration. Then each interrupt
reads 0x10 and, per record, 0x11 (7 bytes: bit 7 down, id, x and y
little-endian; 0x40cc1da4..e34), and hands the points to TPIS, in the
screen's 1024x682.

nikon-z63-touch.h answers those registers: the boot interrupt 10 ms
after power comes on (repeated until read), a report every 16 ms while a
finger is down and one more at the release, the line idling high and
falling for each report. DECLARED, as the chip is not identified: the
timings, flags bit 7 kept set as "ready", scanning while registers 1 and
2 hold 1, version 1.00.00. Fingers come from the new run-time property
touch: qom-set /machine touch 512:341 (or x:y+x:y for two), "" or "up"
to lift. The I2C banks now route through the board: the touch panel at
bank 0/0x55, the posture sensor's endpoint for the rest.

The EXT_INT edge detector put line n at bank n / 16, bit n % 16. The line
records (.data 0xa0280c1b8.., {enable, bank, bit, INTID, ISR, callback})
have nine lines a bank: EXT_INT_0..8 in bank 0, 9..17 in bank 1 bits
0..8. Every line driven so far was in bank 0, so nothing showed it until
the touch panel's EXT_INT_14 never arrived. Fixed.

Checked: after power-on the controller reports ready and scanning starts;
with the camera kept awake (one half-press), a tap at 970:515 opens the
live view's i menu and a tap on its QUAL tile opens image quality. A
touch while the panel is off (standby) is dropped and named.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
